annotations.description:
{{ if $labels.vendor }}Vendor: {{ $labels.vendor }}. Lane: platform, a key API owns. In the last 30 minutes it answered {{ $values.B }} request(s) with a credit refusal: the vendor's own words name spent credit, a spending limit or a 402 (a bare 429 is a rate limit and does not count). Top up the {{ $labels.vendor }} account or rotate to a funded key. The window slides, so this clears about 30 minutes after the last refusal. A person's own key running dry (byo and device lanes) does not page; the dashboard lists it.{{ else }}The credit watch could not run its query (ClickHouse error or the datasource is down), so refusals are not being counted. Open this rule in Grafana and read the error.{{ end }}
Dashboard: https://grafana.example.com/d/api-vendor-credit/?var-ds=ch-k8s-prod
Find the request: the table Recent credit refusals on the dashboard lists each refusal with its request id and the vendor's text. Then: SELECT ts, session_id, status, assistant_reply FROM app_telemetry.request_conversations WHERE request_id_s = '<request id>' (llm_calls and harness_tool_calls key on request_id).

{{ if $labels.vendor }}Vendor: {{ $labels.vendor }}. The edge read the vendor's own balance route and the balance, ${{ printf "%.2f" $values.B.Value }}, is under the minimum for {{ $labels.vendor }} (defaults: modelhub $25, modelhub_chat $25, telnyx $10, fal $25, speechco $10; set per vendor by API_VENDOR_BALANCE_MIN_USD_<VENDOR> on the edge). ModelHub and fal sit in front of many models, so a dry router takes every model behind it down; modelhub_chat is the house-key chat lane's own ModelHub account. Top up the {{ $labels.vendor }} account: ModelHub https://modelhub.example.com/settings/credits (modelhub is the media key's account, modelhub_chat the chat lane's own), Telnyx Mission Control billing, fal dashboard billing, SpeechCo https://console.speechco.example.com billing. This clears on the next poll after the top-up, within 5 minutes. An unknown balance (a 401 or 403, a missing key, a vendor outage) does not page, and one failed poll does not clear a page that stands: the latest balance that was actually read, within the last 20 minutes, decides, and the dashboard row says unknown and why.{{ else }}The balance watch could not run its query (ClickHouse error or the datasource is down), so vendor balances are not being checked. Open this rule in Grafana and read the error.{{ end }}
Dashboard: https://grafana.example.com/d/api-vendor-credit/?var-ds=ch-k8s-prod
Rows: SELECT ts, target, ok, status, ms, error FROM api.probes WHERE target LIKE 'vendor_balance:%' ORDER BY ts DESC LIMIT 20 (ms is the balance in US cents; the edge poller writes one row per vendor every 5 minutes).

{{ if $labels.vendor }}Vendor: {{ $labels.vendor }}. The edge read the vendor's own quota route and what is left, {{ printf "%.0f" $values.B.Value }} {{ $labels.unit }}, is under the minimum for {{ $labels.vendor }} (defaults: voiceco 100000 characters, meshco 500 credits, shapeco 500 credits; set per vendor by API_VENDOR_QUOTA_MIN_<VENDOR> on the edge). VoiceCo speaks the voice replies and MeshCo and ShapeCo build the 3D models, so a dry quota stops that work. Top up or upgrade the {{ $labels.vendor }} plan: VoiceCo https://voiceco.example.com/app/subscription (its characters also reset each month with the plan), MeshCo https://www.meshco.example.com settings, ShapeCo https://platform.shapeco.example.com billing. This clears on the next poll after the top-up, within 5 minutes. An unknown quota (a 401 or 403, a missing key, a vendor outage) does not page, and one failed poll does not clear a page that stands: the latest quota that was actually read, within the last 20 minutes, decides, and the dashboard row says unknown and why.{{ else }}The quota watch could not run its query (ClickHouse error or the datasource is down), so vendor quotas are not being checked. Open this rule in Grafana and read the error.{{ end }}
Dashboard: https://grafana.example.com/d/api-vendor-credit/?var-ds=ch-k8s-prod
Rows: SELECT ts, target, ok, status, ms, error FROM api.probes WHERE target LIKE 'vendor_quota:%' ORDER BY ts DESC LIMIT 20 (ms is what is left in whole units: characters for voiceco, credits for meshco and shapeco; the edge poller writes one row per vendor every 5 minutes).
